  "pre_gate_answer": "# Markdown Briefing\n\n## Summary\n**The retirement system cannot be identified from the provided evidence.** None of the cited investment consultant RFP excerpts includes a requirement that firms certify they currently serve clients with **combined assets of at least $50 billion**.\n\n## Key Findings\n- **No direct match found** for the specific **$50 billion combined-assets certification**.\n- The evidence only shows **similar but different** qualification standards across several retirement systems.\n\n## Relevant Systems Reviewed\n- **Texas Municipal Retirement System (TMRS)**\n  - Requires current service to:\n    - at least **5 public pension plans** larger than **$5 billion**, and\n    - at least **2 public plans** over **$20 billion**\n  - **Not** a combined-assets threshold of **$50 billion**.\n\n- **Employees’ Retirement System of the State of Hawaii (ERS)**\n  - 2017 and 2022 RFPs require experience with public pension clients above certain asset levels\n  - Example: at least one defined benefit public pension client with assets over **$5 billion**\n  - **No** certification tied to **$50 billion combined client assets**.\n\n- **San Diego City Employees’ Retirement System (SDCERS)**\n  - Requires significant experience advising large public pension systems\n  - **No** $50 billion combined-assets certification identified.\n\n- **Anchorage Police and Fire Retirement System**\n  - Requires minimum firm qualifications such as public pension experience and asset thresholds\n  - **No** $50 billion combined-assets requirement found.\n\n- **Boston Retirement System** and **IMRF**\n  - Include general experience and qualification requirements\n  - **No** matching $50 billion certification language shown.\n\n## Conclusion\nBased on the supplied evidence, **the query cannot be answered definitively**. Additional source material containing the exact RFP language would be required to identify the retirement system.",
